Peter <usenet@ointment.org> writes:
> Spoily nurse question:
> 
> So, just out of curiosity :-), is there a formal algorithm used to
> determine whether or not a nurse's blow will result in a hp-gain? I was
> just experimenting a little and it seemed that gains come in waves, and
> seem to have something to do with how long it had been since I had last
> killed something/wielded a weapon...what's the secret??

There will always be an HP gain (d7 HP), unless you're at max HP. If
you're actually asking about a rise in _max_ HP, the chance depends on
your experience level, with diminishing returns:

        if (!rn2(7)) {
            /* hard upper limit via nurse care: 25 * ulevel */
            if (u.uhpmax < 5 * u.ulevel + d(2 * u.ulevel, 10))
                u.uhpmax++;
            if (!rn2(13)) goaway = TRUE;
        }

Any "waves" you're seeing are going to be standard random-distribution
clumping behaviour.

